¤textÙ\And it shall come to pass, that whosoever shall call on the name of the Lord shall be saved.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¿Ye men of Israel, hear these words; Jesus of Nazareth, a man approved of God among you by miracles and wonders and signs, which God did by him in the midst of you, as ye yourselves also know:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†him, being delivered by the determinate counsel and foreknowledge of God, ye have taken, and by wicked hands have crucified and slain:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvwhom God hath raised up, having loosed the pains of death: because it was not possible that he should be holden of it.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses˜„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines“‚¤textÙ"For David speaketh concerning him,¦layout ‚¤textÙ)I foresaw the Lord always before my face,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ7For he is on my right hand, that I should not be moved:¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ7Therefore did my heart rejoice, and my tongue was glad;¦layout ‚¤textÙ*Moreover also my flesh shall rest in hope:¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ,Because thou wilt not leave my soul in hell,¦layout ‚¤textÙ:Neither wilt thou suffer thine Holy One to see corruption.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ,Thou hast made known to me the ways of life;¦layout ‚¤textÙ4Thou shalt make me full of joy with thy countenance.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“Men and brethren, let me freely speak unto you of the patriarch David, that he is both dead and buried, and his sepulchre is with us unto this day.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙµTherefore being a prophet, and knowing that God had sworn with an oath to him, that of the fruit of his loins, according to the flesh, he would raise up Christ to sit on his throne;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„he seeing this before spake of the resurrection of Christ, that his soul was not left in hell, neither his flesh did see corruption.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ<This Jesus hath God raised up, whereof we all are witnesses.¦layout ªlast_verse …¤book+§chapter«first_verse!ªlast_verse$¦verses”„¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¦Therefore being by the right hand of God exalted, and having received of the Father the promise of the Holy Ghost, he hath shed forth this, which ye now see and hear.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙAFor David is not ascended into the heavens: but he saith himself,¦layout ‚¤textÙ6The LORD said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand,¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ$Until I make thy foes thy footstool.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡Therefore let all the house of Israel know assuredly, that God hath made that same Jesus, whom ye have crucified, both Lord and Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse$…¤book+§chapter«first_verse%ªlast_verse)¦verses•„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ”Now when they heard this, they were pricked in their heart, and said unto Peter and to the rest of the apostles, Men and brethren, what shall we do?¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ«Then Peter said unto them, Repent, and be baptized every one of you in the name of Jesus Christ for the remission of sins, and ye shall receive the gift of the Holy Ghost.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ}For the promise is unto you, and to your children, and to all that are afar off, even as many as the Lord our God shall call.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkAnd with many other words did he testify and exhort, saying, Save yourselves from this untoward generation.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~Then they that gladly received his word were baptized: and the same day there were added unto them about three thousand souls.¦layout ªlast_verse)…¤book+§chapter«first_verse*ªlast_verse/¦verses–„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqAnd they continued stedfastly in the apostles' doctrine and fellowship, and in breaking of bread, and in prayers.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTAnd fear came upon every soul: and many wonders and signs were done by the apostles.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ?And all that believed were together, and had all things common;¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXand sold their possessions and goods, and parted them to all men, as every man had need.¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›And they, continuing daily with one accord in the temple, and breaking bread from house to house, did eat their meat with gladness and singleness of heart,¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtpraising God, and having favour with all the people. And the Lord added to the church daily such as should be saved.¦layout ªlast_verse/